Architect ruling: Option (3), adjusted. Close R0 as a route PASS with a known defect. No R0c, and no owner ask.

I reviewed frame-020-4x and the 105 px contact strip. The band is an armpit web: the coat's underside stretches between the torso and the weapon arm during high abduction. This is a textbook local weighting issue for auto-weights on a fused sleeve, not a route problem. The route is validated: a clean AI retopo mesh works with Unity Humanoid avatars and KayKit clips, including a functional handslot sword.

No R0c: this mesh is the free-tier S3 and may not be the final look chosen in G0. Fixing armpit weights now falls into the 'polish before the look is chosen' trap the plan aims to avoid. Fixes only pay off on the selected model.

Record this in the R0 report and §9: "R0 PASS (route), known defect: armpit webbing in high-abduction attacks with fallback auto-weights. Deferred to G3 on the G0-chosen model." In G3, try these in order (one bounded attempt each, stop at the first pass):
(i) Tripo's own rig, if the model comes from Tripo. I'll ask the owner for this at G3, not before.
(ii) KayKit Knight weight transfer for the torso and arms.
(iii) An armpit/shoulder helper bone, or splitting the sleeve.
The G3 PASS rule matches R0b's.

Integration note: approved. Add the rule "candidate prefab and source model must use different Resources keys" to the integration notes on feature/art-g0.

Priority: send the G0 same-fixture sheet to the owner. That's the only open decision. One observation to include in the sheet notes: at 58°, the S3 face appears as a grey, skull-like patch under the helmet. Face readability from above is a G0 judgement point. Don't fix it; just ensure the 4x crop shows it for the owner's review.
